{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-six-more-unusual-traditions-from-six-places/audio/main-151308c22d5c.mp3","durationSec":292.224,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.96,"text":"El Colacho is a tradition in Castrillo de Murcia, a village near Burgos in Spain."},{"start":5.8,"end":9.5,"text":"It began in 1620, so it is more than 400 years old."},{"start":10.18,"end":14.6,"text":"It takes place on the Sunday after Corpus Christi, a Christian celebration."},{"start":16.5,"end":20.2,"text":"In 2026, that Sunday was 7 June."},{"start":20.2,"end":22.68,"text":"The tradition is also called baby jumping."},{"start":23.5,"end":27.16,"text":"Babies born during the past year lie on mattresses in the street."},{"start":27.69,"end":30.4,"text":"A man dressed as the devil jumps over them."},{"start":30.96,"end":33.06,"text":"This man is called El Colacho."},{"start":33.88,"end":35.42,"text":"The jump has a special meaning."},{"start":36.06,"end":38.62,"text":"People believe it takes away bad luck and evil."},{"start":39.54,"end":44.48,"text":"To understand this tradition, remember that the action and the belief belong together."},{"start":45.36,"end":47.56,"text":"It is not simply a jump over mattresses."},{"start":48.86,"end":53.9,"text":"The Battle of the Oranges is the biggest part of the Historic Carnival of Ivrea."},{"start":54.78,"end":58.06,"text":"Ivrea is a town in Piedmont, in northern Italy."},{"start":58.56,"end":61.14,"text":"The event lasts for three days before Carnival ends."},{"start":61.92,"end":64.72,"text":"Teams on foot throw oranges at throwers riding in carts."},{"start":65.8,"end":68.98,"text":"The people throwing on foot are called aranceri."},{"start":68.98,"end":73.66,"text":"There are nine teams on foot, including the Diavoli and the Scacchi."},{"start":73.66,"end":76,"text":"Visitors who do not throw wear a red hat."},{"start":77.1,"end":82.04,"text":"Behind these actions is a story about the people of Ivrea standing up against a cruel ruler."},{"start":82.68,"end":85.3,"text":"The event remembers that story through a shared activity."},{"start":85.82,"end":88.42,"text":"Here, the meaning is different from El Colacho."},{"start":89.26,"end":92.54,"text":"It connects the town's celebration with a story about its people."},{"start":92.54,"end":97.36,"text":"Busójárás is a six-day carnival in Mohács, a town in southern Hungary."},{"start":97.86,"end":99.02,"text":"It happens at the end of winter."},{"start":99.58,"end":106.78,"text":"In 2026, it ran from 12 to 17 February and ended with a big bonfire, a large outdoor fire."},{"start":107.56,"end":111.92,"text":"Men called busós wear scary wooden masks and sheepskin coats."},{"start":112.78,"end":114.5,"text":"These coats are made from sheep's skins."},{"start":115.36,"end":119.42,"text":"The men also carry noisemakers, objects that make loud sounds."},{"start":120.22,"end":124.84,"text":"Masks, warm coats, and noise give this celebration its special character."},{"start":125.54,"end":127.3,"text":"The custom says goodbye to winter."},{"start":128,"end":131.32,"text":"The season is therefore part of its meaning, not just its date."},{"start":132.38,"end":138.18,"text":"In 2009, Busójárás joined UNESCO's list of Intangible Cultural Heritage."},{"start":139.06,"end":145.25,"text":"This list recognises living traditions, including customs that communities continue to practise."},{"start":145.25,"end":151.68,"text":"Onbashira is a festival of Suwa Taisha shrine around Lake Suwa in Nagano, Japan."},{"start":152.4,"end":155.1,"text":"A shrine is a place connected with religious belief."},{"start":155.68,"end":157.84,"text":"The festival is over 1,200 years old."},{"start":158.1,"end":162.2,"text":"It happens in the years of the Tiger and the Monkey, about once every six years."},{"start":162.98,"end":167.04,"text":"It was last held in 2022, and the next festival is in 2028."},{"start":167.88,"end":171.6,"text":"Unlike the other traditions described so far, it is not a yearly event."},{"start":172.5,"end":176.72,"text":"People move 16 huge fir trees from the mountains to the shrine."},{"start":177.46,"end":181.42,"text":"The trees are over 150 years old and about 17 metres tall."},{"start":182.54,"end":184.4,"text":"Riders ride the logs down steep slopes."},{"start":184.98,"end":190.34,"text":"The shrine is at the centre of the festival, and moving these enormous trees is its shared task."},{"start":191.5,"end":194.7,"text":"Tinku is an Andean ritual from northern Potosí in Bolivia."},{"start":195.66,"end":198.78,"text":"A ritual is an activity with a special meaning that people repeat."},{"start":199.48,"end":203.36,"text":"The best-known Tinku takes place in Macha during the Fiesta de la Cruz."},{"start":203.88,"end":207.34,"text":"In 2026, it was on 3 and 4 May."},{"start":208.16,"end":213.04,"text":"Communities come to the town's main square with music, colourful clothes, and dance."},{"start":213.8,"end":216.76,"text":"The ritual is a meeting between two groups of the community."},{"start":217.82,"end":222.88,"text":"People believe it brings a good harvest, meaning a good amount of food gathered from the fields."},{"start":224.42,"end":228.62,"text":"Tinku is also a famous dance at carnival in Oruro."},{"start":228.62,"end":232.72,"text":"Its name therefore connects with both a community ritual and a dance."},{"start":233.94,"end":237.34,"text":"In Macha, hope for the harvest is central to its meaning."},{"start":237.34,"end":242.72,"text":"Thaipusam is a Hindu festival for Lord Murugan, celebrated by Tamil people."},{"start":243.62,"end":247.98,"text":"Its biggest celebration is at Batu Caves, near Kuala Lumpur in Malaysia."},{"start":249.32,"end":252.3,"text":"In 2026, Thaipusam was on 1 February."},{"start":253.58,"end":258.72,"text":"Before the festival, more than 2.5 million visitors were expected at Batu Caves."},{"start":259.42,"end":262.32,"text":"That was an expectation, not a final visitor count."},{"start":263,"end":270.32,"text":"Devotees, people strongly committed to their religion, climb 272 colourful steps to the temple in the cave."},{"start":271.38,"end":275.24,"text":"Many carry a kavadi, a decorated frame, or pots of milk."},{"start":275.24,"end":278.4,"text":"Religious belief is central to this festival."},{"start":279.16,"end":285.58,"text":"The steps, the things people carry, and the temple visit are parts of the celebration for Lord Murugan."},{"start":286.86,"end":291.7,"text":"Understanding that purpose helps us see more than a large crowd or colourful steps."}],"words":[{"text":"El","start":0,"end":0.22},{"text":"Colacho","start":0.22,"end":0.72},{"text":"is","start":0.72,"end":1.08},{"text":"a","start":1.08,"end":1.22},{"text":"tradition","start":1.22,"end":1.52},{"text":"in","start":1.52,"end":1.82},{"text":"Castrillo","start":1.82,"end":2.34},{"text":"de","start":2.34,"end":2.48},{"text":"Murcia","start":2.48,"end":2.88},{"text":"a","start":3.34,"end":3.42},{"text":"village","start":3.42,"end":3.66},{"text":"near","start":3.66,"end":3.96},{"text":"Burgos","start":3.96,"end":4.4},{"text":"in","start":4.4,"end":4.6},{"text":"Spain","start":4.6,"end":4.96},{"text":"It","start":5.8,"end":5.94},{"text":"began","start":5.94,"end":6.3},{"text":"in","start":6.3,"end":6.54},{"text":"1620","start":6.54,"end":7.38},{"text":"so","start":7.72,"end":7.78},{"text":"it","start":7.78,"end":7.86},{"text":"is","start":7.86,"end":7.98},{"text":"more","start":7.98,"end":8.18},{"text":"than","start":8.18,"end":8.38},{"text":"400","start":8.38,"end":8.74},{"text":"years","start":8.74,"end":9.18},{"text":"old","start":9.18,"end":9.5},{"text":"It","start":10.18,"end":10.32},{"text":"takes","start":10.32,"end":10.56},{"text":"place","start":10.56,"end":10.9},{"text":"on","start":10.9,"end":11.22},{"text":"the","start":11.22,"end":11.36},{"text":"Sunday","start":11.36,"end":11.74},{"text":"after","start":11.74,"end":12.1},{"text":"Corpus","start":12.1